{"title":"1992 OIM Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> whose side has length 2, the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed.\n</p><p>a. Show that for every point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the squares of its distances to the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is 5.\n</p><p>b. Show that for every point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> it is possible to construct a triangle whose sides have the lengths of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13fd509f3062449aaea6e10e1040b1d585063f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and that its area is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ce2da9a94e15e4b68d0b8ca5b86bfff6a90f92c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\]\" width=\"24\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1992_OIM_P3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/68/1992_OIM_P3.png/400px-1992_OIM_P3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"312\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/68/1992_OIM_P3.png/600px-1992_OIM_P3.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/68/1992_OIM_P3.png/800px-1992_OIM_P3.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Construct the triangle in the cartesian plane as shown above with the shown vertices coordinates.\n</p><p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> coordinates is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5bb9e87b5769837c0147db6f6ca569080c591af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P_x,P_y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f5b9310541a84b359508aaf4d60e8b012d4069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x^2+P_y^2=r^2=\\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right)^2=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"231\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be the distances from the vertices to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Part a.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f992d730ab2aa09e38cb2adddf9d53b09a6934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2=(P_x-1)^2+\\left( P_y-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3})} \\right)^2=P_x^2+P_y^2-2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"496\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd95a031fd5ad2fa1c4a51eb0a31133ffbb2073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x^2+P_y^2=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4e36e0b1c44f15bb6f3f7d883b4a7d9f3b9ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2=-2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"192\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5ddb0b7c2d55cfb80505f148df74444f168bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2=(P_x-1)^2+\\left( P_y+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3})} \\right)^2=P_x^2+P_y^2+2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"494\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9972e9e79553e8c30a49f7ce496164ad55a4c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2=2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/69697a615c2580b91f464b8dcf6a651479528ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=P_x^2+\\left( P_y-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right)^2=P_x^2+P_y^2-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"384\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/12805dd9dc293f48a53bb7bb24454805aaa0ebae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"139\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09da226501aa813e57d3ee7e0842e1c78611b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2=-2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}+2P_x+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"529\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc888fa45e97ea325e0ba3269d7efe95a597920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9ec757eb559fd9e50a60db77ea8a129838b4fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> cancels in the above equation. So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af39182111bd122f70d4faaa3ae18898df293900.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2=\\frac{15}{3}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" /> Proving proves part a.\n</p><p>Part b.\n</p><p>Using Heron's formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97f34e0c6e6b07c39df0e20b2b7833bacc962d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{a+b+c}{2} \\right)\\left( \\frac{a+b+c}{2} -a\\right)\\left( \\frac{a+b+c}{2} -b\\right)\\left( \\frac{a+b+c}{2} -c\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"558\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c3f71a31b1bab24801546092ed5133105be175b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{\\left( a+b+c \\right)\\left( a+b-c \\right)\\left( a-b+c \\right)\\left( -a+b+c \\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"425\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3afe7e963307bdc562ad13423ca875bc7be8fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{\\left( \\left( a+b \\right)^2-c^2 \\right)\\left(c^2- \\left( a-b \\right)^2 \\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"310\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121bec231132b2c36d0cccc695d559d272c92b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{\\left( \\left( a^2+b^2+c^2 \\right)-2c^2+2ab \\right)\\left( 2c^2-\\left( a^2+b^2+c^2 \\right)+2ab \\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"501\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Substitute what we proved in part a we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97068a624ebfbd5a3d05a42733f1cac66c628e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{\\left( 5-2c^2+2ab \\right)\\left( 2c^2-5+2ab \\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"307\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb8166a67707a91ce091a27d18de7d642d61830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{4a^2b^2-\\left( 2c^2-5 \\right)^2}=\\sqrt{4\\left( a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2 \\right)-25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"433\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>Now let's find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccff768d7fef5fc10a2140c3edf1236220846bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3173a94f0e0b319870f5ca68f85184c200e8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> separately.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9740c7da2a96a180b036e843fd292e927f2819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2=\\left( \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}-2P_x \\right)\\left( \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}+2P_x \\right)=\\left( \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^2-4P_x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"577\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d05fbf3646474605876b85361d0523ba32a772d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2= \\frac{4}{3}P_y^2+\\frac{20}{3\\sqrt{3}}P_y-4P_x^2+\\frac{25}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"270\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now let's find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f14f2bfc283e96633d114ba8fbd0afd5a47650b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-c^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f385be5f720ef591feb4b830d09b8dfb90856067.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^4=\\left(-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^2=\\frac{16}{3}P_y^2-\\frac{40}{3\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{25}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"364\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0baca34582570fdd03e82508bd26c062c4a0ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-c^4=-\\frac{16}{3}P_y^2+\\frac{40}{3\\sqrt{3}}P_y-\\frac{25}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"237\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1448f31a7b16dc88372d0ad257c1a7628b27f8a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/194943d605c1473c6216ac57671b877906579456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5c^2=-\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3efdddaf8a364b56da3098ea6a3e6614a6b014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e882559ed7ee95829493f0d60ccd824b4354a6e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2=\\frac{4}{3}P_y^2+\\frac{20}{3\\sqrt{3}}P_y-4P_x^2+\\frac{25}{9}-\\frac{16}{3}P_y^2+\\frac{40}{3\\sqrt{3}}P_y-\\frac{25}{9}-\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3}}P_y+\\frac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"658\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9ec757eb559fd9e50a60db77ea8a129838b4fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> terms cancel and we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb9f2871929d00f1ee636c1511ce1f0bef70057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2=-4P_y^2-4P_x^2+\\frac{25}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"285\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd95a031fd5ad2fa1c4a51eb0a31133ffbb2073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x^2+P_y^2=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb63ceb06cf7062a9d84f684cb4b4f751e59a45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2=-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{25}{3}=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"247\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418b5979a1dab3589255af09d2da1e85720a5eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b^2-c^4+5c^2=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> into the equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2fc6a1b62724a25224caf98de9a91323d1c6a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df5d544413fd28c6b8720d41dc7fa8fff6b2841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4A=\\sqrt{4\\left(7 \\right)-25}=\\sqrt{28-25}=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"289\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878281fae5938aba9a95a147398677c74187e108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>And since we use Heron's formula, if the triangle was not possible it would have given us imaginary numbers.  Therefore it is now proven that it is possible to construct that triangle and the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b30d7166f38d8f18e66dfd6e9473880efaca2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note.  I actually competed at this event in Venezuela when I was in High School representing Puerto Rico.  I got full points for part a but partial points for part b. because I messed up the algebra on the Heron's formula and couldn't finish the proof.  So, I think I got 6 or 7 points out of 10.</li></ul>\n<p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183446\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 291/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11485/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.191      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.191      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26077:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183446 and revision id 208217. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}